rder-bottom: 1.5px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Ada Kim", "motive": "Helena's field 7 images would prove that the director's ‘variable star’ in three grant applications was invented (clue 5). Ada is the director (clue 2).", "proof": ["The log blames P.NAIR at 23:14 (clue 6), but Priya was on a camera-on video call 200 m away from 22:55 to 23:42 (clue 3), and her code sits on a post-it on the monitor (clue 6).", "Ada says she watched a crystal-clear Jupiter at eleven – but the station shows 8/8 oktas (completely overcast) and heavy rain from 22:50 (clue 2), and Helena paused for clouds at 22:58 (clues 1 and 6).", "At 23:20 a figure with an umbrella left the dome and turned east (clue 4) – and the east path only leads to the director's house (clue 1). The wet footprints fit the rain (clues 1 and 2).", "Only the field 7 images were deleted (clues 1 and 6) – the images that would expose the director (clue 5)."], "cleared": ["Priya was framed with her public code; she was on a video call (clues 3 and 6).", "Ian (rival with a motive) drove to the pub at 22:30 (clue 4).", "Tom and Greta were in the canteen together from 23:00 to 23:40 (clue 4).", "Helena started the run at 22:40 and was at dinner in the village (clue 1)."]}}, {"slug": "the-stolen-final-chapter", "level": 3, "crime": "Theft", "who": "thief", "title": "The Stolen Final Chapter", "teaser": "A crime writer's last manuscript disappears during his own book launch. Two guests lie – but only one is a thief.", "intro": "During the launch party at Greywood Manor, the only copy of crime writer <b>Edmund Grey</b>'s final novel was stolen from his study. Several guests are lying – but not all of them about the theft. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "During the launch party at Greywood Manor, the only copy of crime writer Edmund Grey's final novel was stolen from his study. Several guests are 