color: #FFFFFF; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">6</div></div>\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1E1B18\">Find all 6 clues, then scan the code to name the culprit.</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; width: 250px\">\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #5C554D\">NEXT CLUE IS HIDDEN …</div>\n<div style=\"border-bottom: 1.5px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Raj Malhotra", "motive": "Grapes had been going missing from the top rows all week and Alistair was furious (clue 6). Raj, the winemaker, was the man who could sell them on.", "proof": ["Someone came into the cellar at 9:51 PM with a mortice key and left at 10:04 PM (clue 6). The logger uses the 12-hour clock: that is 21:51 to 22:04.", "Only three people hold mortice keys: Alistair, Raj and Owen (clue 1). Alistair's key was in his pocket, and Owen was ringing up drinks at the bar the whole time (clue 1).", "Raj says he never left the tasting room – but from 21:50 to 22:10 the stage belonged to Celia Marsh's talk (clue 2). He was not needed again until 22:10, which fits the cellar visit exactly."], "cleared": ["<b>Fiona</b> lied about being in bed – she was winning at bingo in St Mary's Hall at 22:02 (clue 3) – and she has no key.", "<b>Celia</b> had a motive (clue 4) but was giving her talk from 21:50 to 22:10 (clue 2).", "<b>Bertie</b> was playing records non-stop (clue 5), and <b>Mags</b> was cutting her birthday cake on the dance floor at 21:58 (clue 5). Neither has a key."]}}, {"slug": "the-ferris-wheel-robbery", "level": 2, "crime": "Theft", "who": "thief", "title": "The Ferris Wheel Robbery", "teaser": "The pier's cash box vanishes from an empty ticket booth. One man was ridi