ed – Lyle was already dead. Hana struck him at 19:11–19:16; the watch only registered the end, after he lay unconscious."], "cleared": ["<b>Kieran</b> came back at 19:31 (clue 3) and fled to the café in shock at 19:34 (clue 4). His story of a silent man with his back turned fits a dead body.", "<b>Bryn</b> quarrelled with Lyle, but sat in F-11 throughout, next to Lily (clue 6).", "<b>Sophie</b> was in the café, and <b>Lily</b> was in her seat."]}}, {"slug": "the-surf-school-drowning", "level": 3, "crime": "Murder", "who": "killer", "title": "The Surf School Drowning", "teaser": "An expert surfer drowns on a calm evening in his own bay. His business partner says she watched the whole thing from the beach – at low tide.", "intro": "In <b>Penhallow Bay</b>, surf-school owner Jake Rowan was found drowned on the rocks at the north end of the beach after an evening paddle. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "In Penhallow Bay, surf-school owner Jake Rowan was found drowned on the rocks at the north end of the beach after an evening paddle. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-18", "daily": "2027-01-03", "public": "2027-01-03", "suspects": [{"name": "Ben Hosking", "role": "Harbour master"}, {"name": "Dan Price", "role": "Instructor"}, {"name": "Elsie Trevan", "role": "Dog walker"}, {"name": "Mo Jansen", "role": "Beach bar owner"}, {"name": "Nina Cole", "role": "Business partner"}, {"name": "PC Morgan Tate", "role": "Police"}], "clues": [{"name": "PC Morgan Tate", "role": "Police", "quote": "Jake had a head wound that the pathologist says came before he went in the water. His dive watch stopped when it flooded – the glass was cracked by a blow.", "label": "POLICE REPORT", "evidence": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px\"><div style=\"font-family: 'Special Elite', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 19px; color: #1E1B18