 size-L left driver's glove was under his body (clue 1).", "Gary says he was driving the whole time, but his tram stopped at the depot gate from 23:10 to 23:25 (clue 3).", "Dev saw a driver jump off tram 9 at 23:12 and return at 23:24 with only his right glove (clue 4). Gary drives tram 9 and wears size L (clues 2 and 3)."], "cleared": ["<b>Tom</b> was at City Square at 23:15 and wears size M (clues 2 and 6).", "<b>Nell</b> was on the radio and wears size S; <b>Dev</b> was gritting outside, and <b>Rosa</b> runs the store (clues 2, 3 and 4)."]}}, {"slug": "murder-at-the-frost-fair", "level": 3, "crime": "Murder", "who": "killer", "title": "Murder at the Frost Fair", "teaser": "The organiser of a winter frost fair is found dead behind the mulled wine stall. Fireworks timing, a card machine and a glove print point to the killer.", "intro": "At the <b>Riverside Frost Fair</b>, organiser Hugh Mercer was found dead behind the mulled wine stall during the fireworks. He had been pushed and hit his head on the iron brazier. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "At the Riverside Frost Fair, organiser Hugh Mercer was found dead behind the mulled wine stall during the fireworks. He had been pushed and hit his head on the iron brazier. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-18", "daily": null, "public": "2026-11-19", "suspects": [{"name": "Clara Mercer", "role": "Hugh's daughter"}, {"name": "DI Kate Marsh", "role": "Police"}, {"name": "Eddie Lamb", "role": "Fireworks technician"}, {"name": "Jill Rowe", "role": "Mulled wine stall holder"}, {"name": "Paul Rowe", "role": "Jill's husband"}, {"name": "Simon Fry", "role": "Chestnut seller"}], "clues": [{"name": "DI Kate Marsh", "role": "Police", "quote": "Witnesses heard a scream behind the stalls just as the first firework went up. The fireworks started exactly at 20:00.", "label": "POLICE REPORT", "evidence