nter; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">6</div></div>\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1E1B18\">Find all 6 clues, then scan the code to name the culprit.</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; width: 250px\">\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #5C554D\">NEXT CLUE IS HIDDEN …</div>\n<div style=\"border-bottom: 1.5px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Lady Fiona Mackie", "motive": "The laird was changing his will to leave the castle to the National Trust instead of Fiona (clue 3).", "proof": ["The goblet was poisoned between the toasts, 20:00–20:30 (clue 1).", "Fiona says she sat at the far end all evening (clues 2 and 3). But at 20:15, while Rev. Small and Mrs Gunn danced, a lady in green velvet with a tartan sash sat in seat 2 and leaned over the laird's goblet (clues 4 and 6).", "Only Fiona wore green velvet (clue 5), and Rev. Small saw her walk back to the far end (clue 6)."], "cleared": ["<b>Mrs Gunn</b> wore blue and was dancing; <b>Rev. Small</b> was dancing too (clues 5 and 6).", "<b>Hamish</b> wore black livery, and <b>Rory</b> was playing in the gallery (clues 4 and 5)."]}}, {"slug": "murder-in-the-city-archive", "level": 3, "crime": "Murder", "who": "killer", "title": "Murder in the City Archive", "teaser": "An archivist is found dead in the vault after finding a document that could ruin a powerful family. A lift log and a pencil catch the killer.", "intro": "At the <b>Redbridge City Archive</b>, archivist Dr Ruth Okoye was found dead in the basement vault, crushed by a moving shelf. She had just found a 1952 land deed that proved the Harrington family's estate was stolen. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intr